@bikestation_HostAddress = http://localhost:5137

### Alle Slots
GET {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/slots
Accept: application/json

### Einzelner Slot
GET {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/slots/2
Accept: application/json

### Messverlauf eines Slots
GET {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/slots/2/readings?limit=20
Accept: application/json

### ESP32 meldet: Fahrrad steht auf Slot 2
POST {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/sensor-data
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 2,
  "pressure": 842,
  "distance": 27,
  "vibration": false
}

### ESP32 meldet: Vibration auf Slot 2
POST {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/sensor-data
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 2,
  "pressure": 842,
  "distance": 27,
  "vibration": true
}

### Offene Alerts
GET {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/alerts
Accept: application/json

### Admin-Login (Admin vorher anlegen: dotnet run -- create-admin <name>)
# @name login
POST {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "HIER-PASSWORT-EINTRAGEN"
}

### Token prüfen
GET {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Alert als erledigt markieren (nur mit Token)
POST {{bikestation_HostAddress}}/api/alerts/1/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

###
